@zeripath 
added the keepalive header as suggested. Didn't help.

Since this affects try.gitea.io also we should not distract ourselves by digging into codeberg specific configs.

The idea behind this makes sense, but I assume that there is some kind of network buffer, so the deadline isn't extended on slow connections, because the buffer isn't cleared on time?

That'd explain our observation, that it's not a fixed timeout - cloning huge repos on a fast connection worked just fine (probably because the buffer is refilled every <5s)? No clue about how this is handled deeper in the code or framework, I was just looking at this specific commit right now.

@zeripath
